From 074f64a0e3c5da230d1aabe81732c5b335e3f29e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:10:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 45/48] bcm2835-gpiod: GPIO pins of the Raspberry Pi as a
 scheme
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

/scheme/gpio/pins lists every pin with mode and level;
/scheme/gpio/<pin>/mode, value and pull read and set one pin. The pins
of the serial console and the SD card are refused.

Refs redox-rpi/redox-rpi#38

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Writing a pull spins for the 10 µs the pull setting needs instead of
sleeping: a 10 µs nanosleep never came back in QEMU.
